; Tutorial_1_User_Interface.inix -- a spoken walk through BatCon, written for buildTutorials (the format is
; described at the top of Tutorial_0_Overview.inix in the Homer kit's Templates).

[about]
Title=1 - User Interface
Intro=The one dialog, control by control, and the keys that reach each one.
Setup=BatCon is installed and your reader is running.
Homework=Open BatCon and visit each control with its Alt key.

[step]
Say=BatCon is one dialog. Alt plus Control plus B, B for BatCon, opens it from anywhere in Windows.
Key=Alt+Control+B
Hear=BatCon dialog
Hear=Source files: edit

[step]
Say=Focus starts in Source files, where you name what to convert: files, folders, or patterns such as star dot P D F.

[step]
Say=Every control has an Alt key: the first letter of its name. Alt plus T, Tango, goes to Target format.
Key=Alt+T
Hear=Target format: list box
Hear=Markdown (md)

[step]
Say=The list shows only the formats every source converts to, each by name, with its extension.

[step]
Say=Alt plus O, Oscar, is Output directory. Left blank, each result goes beside its source.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Output directory: edit, blank

[step]
Say=Three check boxes follow: Include subfolders, Alt plus I; Force replacements, Alt plus F; View output, Alt plus V.
Key=Alt+V
Hear=View output, check box, checked

[step]
Say=Enter, or Control plus Enter from anywhere, presses OK and starts the batch. Escape cancels.

[step]
Say=What this walk taught: Alt plus Control plus B to open BatCon, and Alt with each control's first letter.
